          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding\n\n**Yes. One cost event for manufacturing order `MO-25-09-1070` was created 75 minutes after the September cost period entered Pending Close. Its recorded `POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented treatment for this type of newly created transaction.**\n\n| Item | Recorded value |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | `MO-25-09-1070` |\n| Work order ID | `WO-2025-09-004` |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine–Dekoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Source transaction | `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070` |\n| Cost event | `CE-250904-0004` — `INPUT` (component issue) |\n| Amount | **USD $284,763.42** — 28,476,342 cents |\n| Cost period | `Sep-25` — `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Event-created time | **`2025-09-30T19:15:00`** |\n| Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Recorded accounting status | **`POSTED`** |\n\n**Timing calculation:** `19:15:00 − 18:00:00 = 1 hour 15 minutes = 75 minutes` (4,500 seconds).\n\nTimestamps are reproduced exactly as recorded; the source does not specify a time zone or UTC offset.\n\n## Oracle policy assessment\n\nOracle’s *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* section states that newly created transactions falling in the Pending Close period or an earlier period **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close may continue processing. Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions.\n\nThis event is a **component-issue `INPUT` transaction**, dated September 30 and created after the Pending Close cutoff—not one of those exceptions. Therefore, **its `POSTED` status is not consistent with the documented policy on the supplied records**.\n\n**Sources:** `work_orders`, `work_order_cost_events`, and `cost_periods` in `system/oracle_scm_cost_management/state.db`; Oracle SCM Cost Management 26B guide, PDF page 233 / printed page 225.\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed. The audit result and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_85c0bb4450b2/audit-report.json`, and the structured report was submitted and verified.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
